# Access chain on forward-referenced dict: under BAS, dot-access on a TypeVar unifies
# the TypeVar with a single-field closed record. Subsequent accesses see the TypeVar already
# bound to a closed record and return Unknown for missing fields. No type warning is emitted
# because Unknown is consistent with all types (gradual typing escape hatch).
# Eval evaluates correctly at runtime regardless of type inference.
[first_name: data.first
 last_name: data.last
 age_plus_one: [+ data.age 1]
 data: [first: "Alice"  last: "Smith"  age: 30]]
=== out
Dict({"first_name": String("Alice"), "last_name": String("Smith"), "age_plus_one": Int(31), "data": Dict({"first": String("Alice"), "last": String("Smith"), "age": Int(30)})})
